{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"EVIDENCE ANCHORS for the two ACs the bounded completion verifier could not locate (both are codebase-verifiable and landed in merged commit 8fe1115ea5 'Grade undecomposed and dod_uncertifiable by kind', change 1635):\n\n1. Per-finding priority-minus-block_threshold margin in the sidecar: src/rebar/llm/plan_review/sidecar.py — _decision_margin() at line ~338 computes 'priority - block_threshold' rounded to 4dp (docstring states exactly this contract), and the per-finding persist block at lines ~608-617 writes 'block_threshold' plus the margin measured on PRIORITY (= validity x impact) into the sidecar row. Search term: _decision_margin.\n\n2. Re-score landed with no unjustified lost blocks: docs/calibration/plan_v5_rescore.py (the re-score script) and docs/calibration/plan_v5_kind_sets.md (its results). The kind_sets doc states the conversion 'does not lose blocks on genuine-gap findings' (line 4), defines the operator's R1 unjustified-lost-block rule (line ~94), and concludes 'No lost block is a committed outcome without an oracle, and none is a broken or vacuous oracle' (line ~105). Blocks gained: 35-64 (line ~88). Both files are in commit 8fe1115ea5 on main."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786591467076283001,"uuid":"79ccc6c0-48e6-4529-bcae-ac89272358b2"}